[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-FP-RELATION-LINT
TITLE: Every PARENT_FP entry should have a matching relation
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A node recording a fingerprint for a parent asserts a dependency on that
parent's contract, so it should also carry an edge to it. Nothing enforces
that today, and several nodes in this graph already have a fingerprint with no
corresponding relation.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Without the lint the two can disagree silently, and the edge is what the
traversal follows. A fingerprint the traversal cannot reach is invisible to both
the drift check and the render cache.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Realized as fp-check's "unbacked" case (dev/scripts/fp-check.py) rather than
a separate binary -- the check already walks every PARENT_FP entry against
the node's RELATIONS, so a second pass over the same data would just be the
first one run twice. Its first real run over this repo's own graph found 5
pre-existing violations; see SLICE-FP-DETECTOR's NOTES.
<<<

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-CI-CHECK
TITLE: Gate the design graph in nix flake check
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Add a flake check that exports the graph to JSON and fails on non-zero exit, so
a broken relation or an invalid enum value cannot merge.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Validation currently runs only when someone remembers to run it. The export is
a few seconds on a corpus this size.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
The check must use a clean output directory. Incremental generation produces a
false green: the same broken input exits 1, then 0 on re-run against a warm
output directory.

Determined by SLICE-GRAPH-CHECKS: satisfied as a byproduct, no separate check
added. checks/strictdoc-fp-check.nix (SLICE-FP-DETECTOR) runs `strictdoc
export` under `set -euETo pipefail` inside a clean runCommand $TMPDIR --
validation runs at parse time, so a non-zero export exit already fails that
build. checks/strictdoc-cycle-check.nix (MECH-CYCLE-CHECK) does the same
independently. Two checks now provide this gate; adding a third binary whose
only job was the export step itself would just be the same export run a
third time.
<<<

[SLICE]
UID: SLICE-GRAPH-CHECKS
TITLE: Make the graph fail loud on cycles and on an unvalidated export
DEPTH: verified
AUTHORED_BY: human
STATEMENT: >>>
Two checks over the JSON export, in the harness fp-check already established.

Cycle detection, because StrictDoc's own is blind to relations that carry a
role and every relation here carries one -- a cycle currently surfaces as a
recursion crash during render rather than an error.

An export gate, so a malformed document cannot reach the branch. Determine
first whether checks/strictdoc-fp-check.nix already provides this as a
byproduct of its clean-directory export; if it does, say so and close
MECH-SDOC-CI-CHECK rather than adding a second binary.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Both are small and both close holes that have already been hit. A broken graph
was committed to this branch and the hooks passed it. Cycles have never been
tested because nothing detects them.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Cycle detection: MECH-CYCLE-CHECK. Export gate: determined already satisfied
as a byproduct of checks/strictdoc-fp-check.nix and, now, also of
checks/strictdoc-cycle-check.nix -- see MECH-SDOC-CI-CHECK's NOTES for the
determination. No second export-only binary added.
<<<
RELATIONS:
