[SPIKE]
UID: SPIKE-EXECUTABLE-RULES
TITLE: How much of the design system's rules can run rather than be read
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: run
RETIRES_ON: >>>
An assessment the operator has reviewed answers all four questions -- a grammar
generated from a typed Nix option surface, the state machine and flows that
gate an sdoc's creation and change, validation tiers with measured costs, and
whether the strictdoc package needs a first-party overlay -- and each finding
is either carved into a slice or explicitly declined. A question the assessment
cannot answer is recorded as a node rather than left implicit.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
INV-GUARDS-MUST-EXECUTE records a measured split: every constraint that lived
in a document failed and every executable one held. This spike assesses how
much of the design system's rules can be made to run rather than be read, in
four parts: generating docs/sdoc/grammar.sgra from a typed Nix module with no
untyped escape hatches; modelling the flows that create and change an sdoc as a
state machine, and capturing as nodes whatever resists modelling; tiering
validation by trigger and cost, from the native
traceability_index_build_finished hook to a CLI wrapper built on strictdoc
manage new; and whether any of that needs a first-party strictdoc overlay
rather than the nixpkgs package.

Assessment only. It creates no tasks, does not settle the contract field
selection (MECH-FP-FIELD-TUNING owns that), and does not touch git-flow
handling (MECH-FP-GIT-FLOW-HAZARDS).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The operator has no picture of the state machine and is guessing when asked to
weigh in on it, and the field selection cannot be reviewed as prose either
(DEC-FP-FIELDS-CONFIGURABLE). A measured assessment with a rendered state
machine and a sketched option surface is what turns those guesses into
reviewable decisions.
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
DEC-FP-FIELDS-CONFIGURABLE:0000000
DEC-SYSTEM-PURPOSE:0000000
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Run 2026-08-25. The assessment is held in the operator's working area outside
the repository, with the four finder reports, eight contest files, critic pass,
logs and the Q1 prototype beside it; a fold-in review against two outside
research documents followed the same day. Thirteen agents: one finder per question, a refuter and a defender per report,
one cross-question critic; nine refuter-defender splits are surfaced for the
operator, none adjudicated. RETIRES_ON is not yet met: the operator has not
reviewed it.

Measured, on this corpus with nixpkgs strictdoc 0.27.1. The traceability
index build is 3 ms and the plugin hook body is under 1 ms; the cost of every
command is interpreter and imports 0.4 s, ProjectConfig.default_formats() 0.7
to 1.0 s, and the forkserver parallelizer 1.4 s. Pinning
formats=[SDocFormat(), JSONFormat()] takes export from 3.2 to 1.24 s, manage
new from 3.2 to 1.15 s and format from 3.3 to 1.15 s with a byte-identical
JSON export. The user_plugin hook fires on export, format, manage auto-uid and
server, never on manage new; a Format subclass in formats intercepts every
document read on every command, including manage new, inside the workers. A
hook class defined in strictdoc_config.py crashes every parallelised command
on 0.27.1 until the config inserts its own directory on sys.path.

A typed evalModules surface with no untyped option regenerates grammar.sgra
byte for byte (4085 bytes, 0.03 s): an ordered field catalogue plus per-element
typed subset selection, STATUS the one polymorphic slot. Thirteen of thirteen
bad declarations are rejected only once apply forces the merged value with
deepSeq -- two passed lazily and emitted a plausible grammar before that --
and addCheck's predicate is never called for a submodule in the pinned lib.
strictdoc rejects six of six injected grammar defects, two of them only
through the documents, so the gate exports the corpus and needs no first-party
package.

Of four levels -- node, edge, document, branch -- only the parser and the fp
and cycle checks execute, and only in CI. The parser accepts DEPTH TBD, a
Governed_By pointing at a MECHANISM, and an edit to an accepted decision's
statement. All four hashes reverted in 387cdaec equal today's, so a restored
signature reads as signed and current. Two live violations each of
INV-NO-EXTERNAL-PLAN-REFS and of the role-target table; five definitions of
ready that no two agree on. Ten incidentals logged to 99-backlog.

The package does not need owning for anything questions one or three need.
Seed facts held except: the version delta needs a reqif override plus a
pygments relax; of the six unused nixpkgs-only dependencies only graphviz,
pybtex and setuptools cost closure, the other three return through
html2pdf4doc; the three-derivation claim was found nowhere.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-FP-FIELDS-CONFIGURABLE
  ROLE: Governed_By
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-SYSTEM-PURPOSE
  ROLE: Governed_By
